-- Drops the reader's own picture along with the profile it belonged to.
--
-- The app no longer has a reader to name or to draw: the library, the positions
-- in it and every setting are the device's rather than a person's, so there is
-- nothing left for a portrait to be of. See `ReadingSummary` for what is kept.
--
-- Dropped rather than left in place. It is the one table in this schema that
-- holds a photograph the reader chose from their own device, and keeping
-- kilobytes of somebody's face in a database that nothing reads any more would
-- be the app quietly hoarding it.
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS profile_picture;
